From e78c9b3b55d13be34deb758ed3bd9edee267c86b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:35:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): a turn running outside this window's stream
 keeps its row working [daveey]

A Kanban close-out turn the backend woke in an unopened chat painted the row's
stored outcome (red for a decision) while the agent was still working. The
renderer learns about turns only from its own stream and from the ACTIVE
gateway's session.active_list poll, so a turn in a chat on another gateway
(local while hub is active), or held by another process (SSH-isolated serve,
dashboard, CLI), never reached $sessionDotStateById.

Session list/tree rows now carry `turn_live: true` when the row's lineage holds
a live durable turn lease (state.db session_turn_leases, any process, any
profile; dead holder pids ignored). withRowActivity folds it to 'working', so
the outcome stripe yields to it like any live turn and data-working is set.
